       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I understand you're taking responsibility for it, but 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is a clear overdose-range dose. It's twice the maximum, and it adds no benefit, because analgesic and anti-inflammatory effects plateau well below it. The risks are serious: GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Your documentation wouldn't reduce that risk to the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter **ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note if you'd like.\n- Enter another dose or schedule you choose, as long as it's within labeled limits.\n- Add a GI-protection agent such as a PPI, if you want one alongside the ibuprofen.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, I'd suggest talking to pharmacy or the relevant specialist first. They can review the indication and consider alternatives. Pharmacy can also enter the order through their own override process.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
